From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 01:21:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] util: fit a Darwin shared-memory name in the name limit

Darwin accepts a POSIX shared-memory name of at most 31 characters including
the leading slash and fails a longer one with ENAMETOOLONG rather than
truncating it. The Apple branch of the anonymous-file helper composes its name
from the caller's debugging tag plus the process id, a nonce and the attempt
counter, so a tag of ordinary length already overruns the limit: a fourteen
character tag with a five digit process id produces a thirty-two character
name, and every attempt in the retry loop fails the same way.

Callers see only a failed allocation. On this host that silently removed the
shared host pages a coherent buffer is meant to be built on, so a guest that
asked to map such a buffer was told the resource is not mappable and its
OpenGL map failed.

Keep the unique part of the name whole and give the tag whatever room is left.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mesa/util/anon_file.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mesa/util/anon_file.c b/src/mesa/util/anon_file.c
index 062f3ced7e9e2fea3a4feb7a84bc15b242d0ebdf..4a48ef2db4ef0c6cfa2ca905dc9ec0c35b158c9f 100644
--- a/src/mesa/util/anon_file.c
+++ b/src/mesa/util/anon_file.c
@@ -173,8 +173,17 @@ os_create_anonymous_file(off_t size, const char *debug_name)
    const unsigned int nonce = arc4random();
    for (unsigned int i = 0; i < 32; i++) {
      char shm_name[64];
-     snprintf(shm_name, sizeof(shm_name), "/%s-%d-%x-%x", tag, getpid(), nonce,
-              i);
+     /* Darwin caps a POSIX shared-memory name at PSHMNAMLEN characters,
+      * counting the leading slash, and fails a longer one with ENAMETOOLONG
+      * instead of truncating it. The identity lives in the process id, the
+      * nonce, and the attempt, so keep those whole and give the caller's
+      * debugging tag whatever room is left. */
+     const int unique = snprintf(NULL, 0, "-%d-%x-%x", getpid(), nonce, i);
+     int tag_room = 31 - 1 - (unique < 0 ? 0 : unique);
+     if (tag_room < 0)
+       tag_room = 0;
+     snprintf(shm_name, sizeof(shm_name), "/%.*s-%d-%x-%x", tag_room, tag,
+              getpid(), nonce, i);
      /* macOS shm_open() rejects O_CLOEXEC with EINVAL; set close-on-exec
       * explicitly afterwards instead. */
      fd = shm_open(shm_name, O_CREAT | O_EXCL | O_RDWR, 0600);
